{"complete":true,"date":"2026-10-15","records":[{"id":"2026-10-15:event:c3047c8f41e6ecf7:1","kind":"event","place":"home","source":{"collection":"entries","index":0,"sha256":"c3047c8f41e6ecf72486d658fc4d773fc79b69dfe2637f48fb840ae1d1b0ccbe"},"text":"Morning papers: “Petitions in Supreme Court allege police excesses during Delhi CEC protests” · “What is the Ankita Bhandari case, and why has Rahul Gandhi added weight to her parents’ protest” · “TNPDCL will incur additional cost of ₹5 crore to ₹7 crore per day for purchase of gas power: Nirmal Kumar”","time":"05:57","type":"world"},{"id":"2026-10-15:statement:c59d7d4fc2675978:1","kind":"statement","place":"home","recipient":"Hegel","source":{"collection":"entries","index":3,"sha256":"c59d7d4fc26759784d7557fbb2c13a6461fdf0bebb4ce8f46f0a2edf97ec0874"},"speaker":"Ramesh","time":"06:27","verified":false,"words":"Good morning, sir. The weather is a bit grey, so I have made the tea a little stronger. Would you like breakfast in about thirty minutes?"},{"id":"2026-10-15:statement:1ae5d2429289b82b:1","kind":"statement","place":"home","recipient":"Ramesh","source":{"collection":"entries","index":5,"sha256":"1ae5d2429289b82b5fcb522f4a3af9ce37fdd3594c51fe9b658d235a7f066880"},"speaker":"Hegel","time":"06:27","verified":false,"words":"No, Ramesh, not yet. I shall take my tea here on the step while I read the papers. You may withdraw."},{"id":"2026-10-15:statement:60ece726faace7e9:1","kind":"statement","place":"home","recipient":"Hegel","source":{"collection":"entries","index":6,"sha256":"60ece726faace7e9107c3c16268cf4e4e880e35aba2c9a1b2ae14a062d4d7171"},"speaker":"Ramesh","time":"06:27","verified":false,"words":"Yes, sir. The step is dry enough, I have put a towel down. I will be in the kitchen if you need anything."},{"id":"2026-10-15:statement:1606d3772725ff39:1","kind":"statement","place":"home","recipient":"Ramesh and Shri G. Hegde","source":{"collection":"entries","index":8,"sha256":"1606d3772725ff391137942e6c32ae865d385ded245af69f5d93447e50efeaf3"},"speaker":"Hegel","time":"06:32","verified":false,"words":"Shri Hegde, the confusion of our names is a matter of administrative error, yet you stand in my house. I trust you will make yourself comfortable in the second bedroom, pending the Directorate's orders, and that we may maintain a civilized silence in one another's presence."},{"id":"2026-10-15:statement:f77858aea2660514:1","kind":"statement","place":"home","recipient":"Hegel","source":{"collection":"entries","index":9,"sha256":"f77858aea26605144d3eec2ad4a7c278d3fb7fb71d689ba815dc38c2ed938294"},"speaker":"Shri G. Hegde","time":"06:32","verified":false,"words":"I am not staying in your house, sir. I am staying in my allotted room, as per the order you are apparently ignoring. Please do not call it a civilized silence; call it a boundary."},{"id":"2026-10-15:statement:803b47dc2ecf7b17:1","kind":"statement","place":"home","recipient":"Ramesh and Shri G. Hegde","source":{"collection":"entries","index":11,"sha256":"803b47dc2ecf7b17a5c579f85950e49962949f374e3741566f1901897c7265b0"},"speaker":"Hegel","time":"06:47","verified":false,"words":"Shri Hegde, you mistake the nature of the error. The Directorate’s mistake is a defect in the administration, not a moral failing on my part. I am not ignoring your order; I am awaiting the correction of a clerical error that placed me in your shoes. As for your boundary, I note it, but I do not accept that my presence constitutes an intrusion. We are both subjects of the state, and the state’s will, however confused, places us here. Let us not elevate a paperwork error to a metaphysical dispute."},{"id":"2026-10-15:statement:983f77776c1e50ad:1","kind":"statement","place":"home","recipient":"Hegel","source":{"collection":"entries","index":12,"sha256":"983f77776c1e50add1e2b05583b8324b11c7042c871d3425558bf719c9e98665"},"speaker":"Shri G. Hegde","time":"06:47","verified":false,"words":"Metaphysical? No, sir, it’s just my kitchen and my sleep. You can wait in the car till the clerk fixes his file; I won’t be moving for him."},{"id":"2026-10-15:statement:650c4a0b33a7f5e3:1","kind":"statement","place":"lodhi","recipient":"Hegel","source":{"collection":"entries","index":15,"sha256":"650c4a0b33a7f5e359684d95966f292326afe65e891fcda64fd52df145736b5b"},"speaker":"Sunil","time":"08:07","verified":false,"words":"Oh, it’s you again. Same time, same place, same tired face? I’ve got the kettle just starting to rumble, so if you want, I can put a cup out before the crowd gets thick."},{"id":"2026-10-15:statement:32bca494cf86546c:1","kind":"statement","place":"lodhi","recipient":"Mr. R. K. Malhotra and Sunil","source":{"collection":"entries","index":17,"sha256":"32bca494cf86546ca9426655e4ef282c7b45088fb20173d66fe0f5c8dd89294d"},"speaker":"Hegel","time":"08:07","verified":false,"words":"Yes, Sunil. One cup, please. The same as always."},{"id":"2026-10-15:statement:f502c5fc6cbeacce:1","kind":"statement","place":"lodhi","recipient":"Hegel","source":{"collection":"entries","index":18,"sha256":"f502c5fc6cbeacceb6f46708ae4dde8826d6c38810b5fff946874551440d344f"},"speaker":"Sunil","time":"08:07","verified":false,"words":"Haan, same as always. Twenty rupees, bhai. You’re lighter than usual today, or is it just the overcast?"},{"amount":20,"canonical_id":null,"creditor":null,"direction":"out","id":"2026-10-15:payment:74a3885377aee4e4:1","item":"Chai from the stall at the Lodhi Road gate","kind":"payment","medium":"cash","payer":null,"place":"lodhi","settled":true,"source":{"collection":"entries","index":19,"sha256":"74a3885377aee4e45903292b8bed80f49bc18ca565c90d380f11feb73182dde0"},"time":"08:07"},{"id":"2026-10-15:statement:1be9f267e059b8c4:1","kind":"statement","place":"lodhi","recipient":"Sunil","source":{"collection":"entries","index":21,"sha256":"1be9f267e059b8c4cb8f5f9b9ee3f39a039dd7d1a3930b02a668c8589ca75f12"},"speaker":"Hegel","time":"08:17","verified":false,"words":"It is the overcast, Sunil. The day is dismissed early, as is proper. Thank you."},{"id":"2026-10-15:statement:da55d4dac217fa45:1","kind":"statement","place":"lodhi","recipient":"Hegel","source":{"collection":"entries","index":22,"sha256":"da55d4dac217fa45d66a1f80854047b15e6a9b995fca8d70b77dd14e4e45f565"},"speaker":"Sunil","time":"08:17","verified":false,"words":"Proper, aap keh rahe ho? Haan, sky is grey, so maybe the mood is grey too. Drink hot, the mist will settle by ten."},{"id":"2026-10-15:statement:36286e7e94931592:1","kind":"statement","place":"lodhi","recipient":"Sunil","source":{"collection":"entries","index":24,"sha256":"36286e7e94931592148b5e9e9f1fa0a114f3f8394accf110ec5af7eaff376791"},"speaker":"Hegel","time":"08:27","verified":false,"words":"The mist is the veil of the infinite, Sunil. It does not settle because it is good, but because the day demands its form. I shall walk the tombs while the air is cool."},{"id":"2026-10-15:statement:38843fe11e7818fc:1","kind":"statement","place":"lodhi","recipient":"Hegel","source":{"collection":"entries","index":25,"sha256":"38843fe11e7818fca84bffc02c1873bfe87b59d49333d0bd7cc1113c49879936"},"speaker":"Sunil","time":"08:27","verified":false,"words":"Veil, infinite, form... aap toh philosopher lagte ho, not a chai drinker. Walk your tombs, but don't drop my cup on the grass. I'll be here if you get thirsty again."},{"amount":20,"canonical_id":null,"creditor":null,"direction":"out","id":"2026-10-15:payment:7869042b501b6cb3:1","item":"Chai from the stall at the Lodhi Road gate","kind":"payment","medium":"cash","payer":null,"place":"lodhi","settled":true,"source":{"collection":"entries","index":26,"sha256":"7869042b501b6cb36e260ece47725ff50d13baf3389d1042714d7f8c6c208b44"},"time":"08:27"},{"id":"2026-10-15:statement:c968a1de24b93903:1","kind":"statement","place":"home","recipient":"Ramesh","source":{"collection":"entries","index":29,"sha256":"c968a1de24b939037b30dff426411256247c45cb524741cd97d2520d590062bb"},"speaker":"Hegel","time":"08:57","verified":false,"words":"Ramesh, the house is sufficient for the moment. See that the study is aired out; the books require a cool room, and I shall be there until the heat, or the absence of it, becomes bearable. Do not disturb me."},{"id":"2026-10-15:statement:ad481c2bed282912:1","kind":"statement","place":"home","recipient":"Hegel","source":{"collection":"entries","index":30,"sha256":"ad481c2bed282912d0bb65b83318b01e0c84c2c3c57cc1b890082b65888ee9a3"},"speaker":"Ramesh","time":"08:57","verified":false,"words":"Yes, sir. I will open the windows and check the curtains. You won't find me in the way."},{"id":"2026-10-15:statement:ced13cd7d7897e45:1","kind":"statement","place":"home","recipient":"Ramesh","source":{"collection":"entries","index":33,"sha256":"ced13cd7d7897e451e088041bf6056d610c58d0e11fa906339743942ef6f3ae3"},"speaker":"Hegel","time":"10:12","verified":false,"words":"Ramesh, leave me to my thoughts. The house is quiet enough."},{"id":"2026-10-15:statement:cd6eaaccbbac7e9e:1","kind":"statement","place":"home","recipient":"Hegel","source":{"collection":"entries","index":34,"sha256":"cd6eaaccbbac7e9ea8f15e535e71dfcf9d687bafe249991284c04a24ec89d87d"},"speaker":"Ramesh","time":"10:12","verified":false,"words":"Yes, sir."},{"id":"2026-10-15:statement:88c36ddd190caf1c:1","kind":"statement","place":"home","recipient":"Ramesh","source":{"collection":"entries","index":37,"sha256":"88c36ddd190caf1cdf9983469a0faaf80d5a6e2de697442cd3ae7f6d2a19987c"},"speaker":"Hegel","time":"12:12","verified":false,"words":"Ramesh, prepare the plate you mentioned: the omelette, the toast, and the pot of tea. I am hungry, and the body must be attended to before the spirit can continue its work."},{"id":"2026-10-15:statement:0590c1e4857b2740:1","kind":"statement","place":"home","recipient":"Hegel","source":{"collection":"entries","index":38,"sha256":"0590c1e4857b274014cae05f69b74621aa8decc59fb24cf7bb07f01e62b82a8a"},"speaker":"Ramesh","time":"12:12","verified":false,"words":"Yes, sir. I’ll have it ready in twenty minutes."},{"id":"2026-10-15:event:4a69e6277f7d275b:1","kind":"event","place":"home","source":{"collection":"entries","index":40,"sha256":"4a69e6277f7d275be2fa4429cb84d57effb0b24a97db1cdc05b9ab53d6cc7ca6"},"text":"Ramesh brings tea.","time":"16:42","type":"world"},{"id":"2026-10-15:event:be6b3c9fe760cd6e:1","intended_time":"06:30","kind":"event","place":null,"source":{"collection":"plan.items","index":0,"sha256":"be6b3c9fe760cd6ea63b82c6764413b71d8a13c953eab91141bf37ce1eb169c5"},"status":"planned","text":"Read the newspapers on the step to observe the state of public opinion.","time":"05:57","type":"intention"},{"id":"2026-10-15:event:e196cb356be1028c:1","intended_time":"08:00","kind":"event","place":null,"source":{"collection":"plan.items","index":1,"sha256":"e196cb356be1028c9abbaef3b96e3475c23f6829b1b0be9b4b382ab7f191dc64"},"status":"planned","text":"Walk to Lodhi Gardens to study the tombs and the morning light.","time":"05:57","type":"intention"},{"id":"2026-10-15:event:882c219ace1aa446:1","intended_time":"11:00","kind":"event","place":null,"source":{"collection":"plan.items","index":2,"sha256":"882c219ace1aa44684d681f2b5eee7e71274e3c2b98d7a66f4ef47c2e4211bcf"},"status":"planned","text":"Return home to rest and contemplate the dialectic of the Indian spirit.","time":"05:57","type":"intention"},{"id":"2026-10-15:event:deea0221c261f192:1","intended_time":"14:00","kind":"event","place":null,"source":{"collection":"plan.items","index":3,"sha256":"deea0221c261f1929e3a594bda72c7ddee4801e2b76ee029327f5cf292ac121b"},"status":"planned","text":"Draft a letter to the Directorate regarding the pending vouchers.","time":"05:57","type":"intention"},{"id":"2026-10-15:event:b8055957b578a8d2:1","intended_time":"17:00","kind":"event","place":null,"source":{"collection":"plan.items","index":4,"sha256":"b8055957b578a8d272896b595a4221778ec5025ee24688c58bdc364ff3c265b5"},"status":"planned","text":"Take a short walk in the compound to exercise the body.","time":"05:57","type":"intention"},{"id":"2026-10-